### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Orgcraft — end-to-end happy path
### Run top-to-bottom. Each request feeds ids to the next via {{...}}.
### The HTTP client keeps the login session cookie automatically,
### so run #1 and #2 first, then the rest in order.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@host = http://127.0.0.1:8080
@slug = acme
@founderEmail = al@acme.com
@founderPassword = Password@123

### 1. Register organization (public, no auth)
### Creates org + founder user, and writes organization:{id}#admin@user:{founder}
POST {{host}}/api/v1/organizations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Acme Inc",
  "slug": "{{slug}}",
  "founderFirstName": "Al",
  "founderLastName": "Founder",
  "founderEmail": "{{founderEmail}}",
  "founderPassword": "{{founderPassword}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("orgId", response.body.organizationId);
    client.global.set("founderId", response.body.founderId);
    client.log("orgId=" + response.body.organizationId + "  founderId=" + response.body.founderId);
%}

### 2. Login as the founder (tenant = slug). Establishes the session cookie.
POST {{host}}/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

email={{founderEmail}}&password={{founderPassword}}&tenant={{slug}}

### 3. Create a second user (authenticated)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Bob",
  "lastName": "Member",
  "email": "bobo@acme.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("userId", response.body.id);
    client.log("userId=" + response.body.id);
%}

### 4. Create a team → writes team:{id}#creator@user:{founder} + team:{id}#organization@organization:{org}
POST {{host}}/api/v1/teams
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Platform" }

> {%
    client.global.set("teamId", response.body.id);
    client.log("teamId=" + response.body.id);
%}

### 5. Add the user to the team → writes team:{id}#member@user:{user}
POST {{host}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/members
Content-Type: application/json

{ "teamId": "{{teamId}}", "userId": "{{userId}}" }

### 6. Create an office → writes office:{id}#creator@user:{founder} + office:{id}#organization@organization:{org}
POST {{host}}/api/v1/offices
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Rome Office",
  "address": { "address": "Via Roma 1", "city": "Rome", "country": "Italy" }
}

> {%
    client.global.set("officeId", response.body.id);
    client.log("officeId=" + response.body.id);
%}

### 7. Assign the user to the office → writes office:{id}#occupant@user:{user}
POST {{host}}/api/v1/offices/{{officeId}}/members
Content-Type: application/json

{ "officeId": "{{officeId}}", "userId": "{{userId}}" }

### ── Reads ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Users
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users

### Teams
GET {{host}}/api/v1/teams

### Team members
GET {{host}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/members

### Offices
GET {{host}}/api/v1/offices

### Office members (current occupants)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/offices/{{officeId}}/members

### User office history
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/office-history

### ── Cleanup (optional — each delete removes the matching SpiceDB tuples) ──

### Remove user from team → deletes team:{id}#member@user:{user}
DELETE {{host}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/members/{{userId}}

### Delete team → deletes all team:{id} tuples
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/teams/{{teamId}}

### Remove user from office → deletes office:{id}#occupant@user:{user}
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/offices/{{officeId}}/members/{{userId}}

### Delete office → deletes all office:{id} tuples
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/offices/{{officeId}}
